# Topics for fpga_summary.pdf (FPGA Prototyping by VHDL Examples, exam summary):
# which pages are about which Wire part, chip or circuit.
#
#   page[-last]  Title of the section  :  patterns
#
# A pattern is a part kind (and, nand, mux, dff, counter, ram, tri ...), or the
# name of a chip or circuit file; * matches anything (*alu* matches alu and
# my_alu). Sections are listed in the order written here, and the first one
# that matches is the page opened.

# ---- gates
9      The basic gates and their truth tables           : gates and or nand nor xor xnor not buf
9      Universal gates: everything from NAND or NOR     : gates nand nor
7      Boolean algebra (De Morgan, SOP and POS)         : and or nand nor xor xnor not
8      Karnaugh maps                                    : and or nand nor not
10     Timing of real gates: propagation delay          : and or nand nor xor xnor not buf
10     74xx chips worth recognising                     : and or nand nor xor xnor not buf
9-10   Logic families: TTL and CMOS                     : not buf

